; An inline GROUP as the sole entry of a MAP-rep group-choice arm (`{ (a: uint) // b: tstr }`) is
; rejected gracefully (`an inline group ... in entry position is unsupported`, parsing.rs
; `group_entry_to_type`) rather than aborting the run. Naming the group (`g = (a: uint)`, then
; `t = { g // b: tstr }`) is the spelling the rejection points at, verified to generate under both
; the default and the `--preserve-encodings` profile. This fixture pins the MAP rep: the matrix
; containment axis carries the array-rep spelling of the same construct, and no cell expresses this
; one. The message itself is pinned by `inline_group_choice_arm_rejects_gracefully` in
; src/tests/robustness_tests.rs.
t = { (a: uint) // b: tstr }
